    "calibrated_from": [
      "Philips DigitalDiagnost C50, 6 scans: Export_2026-07-27_10-00-05_1 (2 images) and Export_2026-07-30_14-23-58_1 (4 images), covering 3 phantom orientations (0 deg, 90 deg, 180 deg)."
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Canonical frame: origin at phantom-face center, +x right / +y up in the guide-figure orientation; units mm.",
      "Absolute scale anchored to the tape-measure pitch (5.0 mm nominal); side_mm=299.5 makes the measured pitch read 5.000 mm.",
      "nominal_side_mm=300.0 is ASSUMED design intent (no drawing available); measured mean side 299.3-299.9 mm.",
      "Wedge steps are labeled S1 (top, most attenuating) .. S7 (bottom) BY POSITION; no material or thickness values are assumed.",
      "Low-contrast circles are labeled L1..L8 in design order of increasing measured contrast (boustrophedon starting top-right). Grid measured at u = +/-10, +/-30 mm and v = +9.4 / -10.2 mm in block coordinates; measured contrasts run ~0.33 % (L1) to ~1.37 % (L8) at 77 kV. No nominal contrast values are assumed.",
      "Line-pair group positions/frequencies are MEASURED per scan at runtime (band-limited periodicity map); the values here are nominal search seeds only.",
      "Wedge step boundaries measured (steps are ~19 mm, bottom step ~26 mm; not uniform).",
      "IMPORTANT - two phantom variants observed. The scans split into two groups (detector labels HmmEi and A8Tgg) whose internal features sit up to ~12 mm apart and whose strip angle differs by ~3 deg (44.9 vs 48.2). Positions stored here are the mean of the two; per-scan measurement absorbs the difference. Do not treat these nominals as design intent.",
      "Wedge response is reproducibly S-shaped (linear R^2 ~0.92 in all six scans with a near-identical residual pattern). R^2 is therefore a shape descriptor with a soft 0.85 warn threshold; the hard criteria are monotonicity and non-saturation.",
      "Line-pair ROIs are placed at roi_angle_offset_deg (45 deg) from the strip axis, so their corners align with the nub markers on the frame lines and the strip centre line, as the guide specifies.",
      "Wedge step ROIs are a FIXED roi_w_mm x roi_h_mm for every step, so the same step is comparable between phantoms; the printed steps are not equal heights."
    ]
